cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this was useful in your work, please cite it."
title: "Reproducing a low-dose CT baseline from the forward operator up, then beating it with a paired test"
abstract: "Low-dose CT reconstruction built from a GPU Radon transform with an autodiff adjoint: a scoring harness that owns the ground truth, a parametrized family of operator mismatches with guards that must fail on deliberately broken operators, and a search loop that proposes variants and confirms them on held-out data. The reproduction is carried to the point where the seven differences between the method as described and the method as run are written down. A TGV variant found by the loop beats the matched TV recipe by 0.70 +/- 0.04 dB, paired on 128 held-out images, winning on 125. The first published version of the table was wrong and the correction is kept in place."
type: software
